Touch edge rejection for KWin 6.7.5 (branch touchscreen-edge-rejection in
~/Workspace/src/kwin, not upstream): a touch that starts closer than a
per-device width to an edge of a touch screen is held back until it moves
more than 3 mm, and dropped when it ends before that. The width is the
InputDevice D-Bus property touchEdgeRejectionWidth (TouchEdgeRejectionWidth
in kcminputrc, 0 to 10 mm, default 0 = off).

Generated with: git diff v6.7.5 touchscreen-edge-rejection-6.7.5 -- . ':!autotests'
in ~/Workspace/src/kwin-6.7.5 (the tests ran on that branch; the ebuild has
RESTRICT="test"). Applies with -p1 to kwin-6.7.5.tar.xz after
kwin-6.7.5-patchset-1.

